{
 "about": "Pattern learning (lab/pattern_learn.py, 2.93). Mandeep, 23 Nov 2026: 'patterens to observe karte raho or ye dekhna hai humein ki system patterens achhe se pakdna seekhe toh do the best'. Every candle pattern occurrence is described by its situation (the dims below) and the system learns, per pattern, which situations make it pay after costs: the pattern's own average plus each situation's difference from it, shrunk toward zero by shrink_k occurrences (a few lucky trades cannot decide). Days are split train / validation / holdout; the pick (top x% quality) is chosen on validation; every number shown is from the holdout days. Sources: 'lab' = years of 5-minute history in the Strategy Lab's bar table (the ATM option bought its way, real option prices, every cost: pnl_<exit> / premium; and, learned separately, whether the price itself moved the pattern's way in the next fwd_bars bars: 'caught', judged by catch_bar_pct / catch_lift_pct) and 'bench' = the live test bench (every timeframe, honest 1-lot fills, R after costs). Live (shadow): each candle pattern the test bench takes gets its quality 0-100 in its bench record (tag pq); the forward check compares high-quality patterns with all of them on days after the model was built. Nothing here alerts, trades or changes a paper account.",
